From: Marco Sumari Tellez <ing.sumari@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] add_test: const-correct the version-string scanners

test_api_version() scans two const strings returned by
dwg_api_version_string() and dwg_api_so_version(), but holds the results
of strchr() in plain `char *`. GCC 15 diagnoses the lost qualifier and,
because the test suite builds with -Werror, `make check` fails to compile
before a single test runs:

  add_test.c:1296:6: error: assignment discards 'const' qualifier from
      pointer target type [-Werror=discarded-qualifiers]

d0/d1/d2 are only ever read (assert, &d0[1], atoi), so making them const
is enough; no cast and no copy needed.

With this, `make check` on 0.14.8556 is 270 PASS / 0 FAIL on
Ubuntu with gcc 15.2.0.
---
diff --git a/test/unit-testing/add_test.c b/test/unit-testing/add_test.c
--- a/test/unit-testing/add_test.c
+++ b/test/unit-testing/add_test.c
@@ -1283,7 +1283,7 @@ test_api_version (void)
 {
   const char *version = dwg_api_version_string ();
   long i0, i1, i2;
-  char *d0, *d1, *d2;
+  const char *d0, *d1, *d2;
   const int major = dwg_api_version_major ();
   const int minor = dwg_api_version_minor ();
 
